ANALYSIS:
- evtest ran only briefly (Ctrl-C after a few seconds)
- Kernel doesn't log every lid state change by default — they go
  straight to /dev/input/event0 consumed by systemd-logind
- Would need persistent logger running for hours/days to catch
  sporadic event

Proposed (but not applied) persistent lid logger script:
  cat > /usr/local/bin/lid-logger.sh << 'EOF'
  #!/bin/bash
  evtest /dev/input/event0 2>&1 | while read line; do
    echo "$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S.%N') $line"
  done >> /var/log/lid-events.log
  EOF

